# file-write

Creates a new file or modifies an existing file with the specified content.

## Description

The `file-write` command allows you to create new files or modify existing ones by specifying the file path and the content to write. By default, it will not overwrite existing files unless explicitly instructed to do so with the `--overwrite` flag.

## Usage

```
> file-write <file_path> <content> [--overwrite=true|false]
```

## Arguments

- `file_path` (required): The path of the file to create or modify
- `content` (required): The content to write to the file

## Flags

- `--overwrite` (optional): Whether to overwrite an existing file if it exists (default: false)

## Examples

Create a new text file:
```
> file-write myfile.txt "Hello, World!"
```

Create or overwrite a JSON configuration file:
```
> file-write config.json '{"key": "value"}' --overwrite=true
```

## Notes

- The command will automatically create any directories in the path if they don't exist
- The content is written exactly as provided, with no automatic formatting
- Use quotes around the content if it contains spaces or special characters

```javascript
async function execute(args, flags) {
  try {
    // Parse arguments
    const filePath = args[0];
    const content = args[1];
    
    // Validate required arguments
    if (!filePath) {
      return {
        status: "error",
        message: "❌ Error: Missing required argument: file_path"
      };
    }
    
    if (content === undefined) {
      return {
        status: "error",
        message: "❌ Error: Missing required argument: content"
      };
    }
    
    // Parse overwrite flag
    const overwrite = flags.overwrite === "true";
    
    // Check if file exists
    const fileExists = await checkFileExists(filePath);
    
    if (fileExists && !overwrite) {
      return {
        status: "error",
        message: `❌ Error: File '${filePath}' already exists. Use --overwrite=true to overwrite it.`
      };
    }
    
    // Create directories if needed
    const dirPath = filePath.substring(0, filePath.lastIndexOf("/"));
    if (dirPath) {
      await createDirectory(dirPath);
    }
    
    // Write the file
    await writeFileContent(filePath, content);
    
    return {
      status: "success",
      message: `✅ Successfully wrote to file: ${filePath}`
    };
  } catch (error) {
    return {
      status: "error",
      message: `❌ Error writing file: ${error.message}`
    };
  }
}

async function checkFileExists(filePath) {
  const result = await editFile({
    target_file: filePath,
    instructions: "Check if file exists without modifying it",
    code_edit: ""
  }).catch(() => null);
  
  return !!result;
}

async function createDirectory(dirPath) {
  await runTerminalCmd({
    command: `mkdir -p ${dirPath}`,
    is_background: false
  });
}

async function writeFileContent(filePath, content) {
  await editFile({
    target_file: filePath,
    instructions: "Write content to file",
    code_edit: content
  });
}
```